01:46:02,208 --> 01:46:06,908
'cause like I said, I don't really have any plans to get going anytime soon.

1845
01:46:07,508 --> 01:46:11,508
But I guess the way that I feel about it is...

1846
01:46:11,908 --> 01:46:16,908
I'd like to keep remembering all those people and things that we did fondly,

1847
01:46:17,108 --> 01:46:18,508
regardless of anything.

1848
01:46:18,908 --> 01:46:21,708
Even through the years, and though they may pass by,

1849
01:46:21,808 --> 01:46:24,308
and even when the wounds aren't fresh anymore,

1850
01:46:24,708 --> 01:46:27,508
I still... I still want to remember.

1851
01:46:27,808 --> 01:46:30,708
I know it's hard to move forward sometimes

1852
01:46:30,808 --> 01:46:36,108
when the things that we love and care about are still behind us, right?

1853
01:46:36,708 --> 01:46:38,908
Stuck in the past, but...

1854
01:46:39,208 --> 01:46:43,508
I'm going to be here to make you smile no matter what.

1855
01:46:44,508 --> 01:46:48,508
Right now, there's still stuff I want to do, you know?

1856
01:46:48,708 --> 01:46:50,508
And yeah, that's a good point.

1857
01:46:50,608 --> 01:46:52,908
Good memories, they should make you sad,

1858
01:46:53,008 --> 01:46:55,708
because that means they were truly good.

1859
01:46:56,208 --> 01:46:59,808
We did a lot of really good stuff, don't you think?

1860
01:47:00,808 --> 01:47:06,708
Well... I'm glad that I sang that here with Ina. I'm really glad.

1861
01:47:07,008 --> 01:47:09,208
But there's still some people that I haven't sung with,

1862
01:47:09,308 --> 01:47:12,208
so let's head to the final area, shall we?

1863
01:47:12,508 --> 01:47:15,508
What if I just... bam! Teleported myself there?

1864
01:47:15,808 --> 01:47:17,908
And use my crazy powers of...

1865
01:47:18,008 --> 01:47:19,608
Oh, my waist is broken.

1866
01:47:19,708 --> 01:47:23,108
That's okay. No, it's fine. All good, all good.

1867
01:47:23,208 --> 01:47:25,708
I probably just need to T-pose real quick. Hang on, watch this.

1868
01:47:25,808 --> 01:47:27,908
Watch my sick T-pose.

1869
01:47:28,008 --> 01:47:30,208
Hang on. I'm already good at this.

1870
01:47:30,308 --> 01:47:32,808
I've become a pro at VR Chat in just this short time.

1871
01:47:33,508 --> 01:47:36,508
There we go. Fixed!

1872
01:47:36,808 --> 01:47:39,508
All right. Time to summon my persona

1873
01:47:39,608 --> 01:47:41,808
and head to the final area!

1874
01:47:41,908 --> 01:47:44,908
Oh! We're here! We're here!

1875
01:47:45,008 --> 01:47:49,308
Oh, where'd my camera go? I lost it.

1876
01:47:49,508 --> 01:47:52,708
Is it hiding... Is it behind me?

1877
01:47:52,808 --> 01:47:57,708
Oh, I found it! There you are! I found you!

1878
01:47:58,808 --> 01:48:01,908
Um, this is one of my favorite areas, I think.

1879
01:48:02,008 --> 01:48:04,308
You guys... You guys, look!

1880
01:48:04,408 --> 01:48:06,708
What is this? Green fields?

1881
01:48:06,808 --> 01:48:09,508
Oh, there's one of those camera thingies. Hang on, okay.

1882
01:48:09,708 --> 01:48:11,908
Check this out.

1883
01:48:12,708 --> 01:48:16,908
Whoa! It's too beautiful!

1884
01:48:17,208 --> 01:48:19,908
Can you guys imagine hanging out with your friends here?

1885
01:48:20,008 --> 01:48:22,208
Wouldn't that be so awesome?

1886
01:48:22,308 --> 01:48:26,508
I'm running up that hill. I'm running up the hill. Oh, my gosh!

1887
01:48:27,208 --> 01:48:30,208
Wait a minute. What's this?

1888
01:48:31,208 --> 01:48:33,908
Was Ina painting something here?

1889
01:48:34,008 --> 01:48:36,208
I didn't know about that. Heh.

1890
01:48:36,308 --> 01:48:39,408
I mean, it is a really nice scenery to paint, I suppose.

1891
01:48:39,508 --> 01:48:43,508
Yeah, I guess it makes sense. I'd want to paint here.

1892
01:48:43,708 --> 01:48:47,508
So expansive. Oh, sorry, from the sun. Oh, that's okay. It doesn't matter. Um...

1893
01:48:47,908 --> 01:48:50,508
So surreal and tranquil.

1894
01:48:50,808 --> 01:48:54,908
I guess this is a good place to tell you guys the news about...

1895
01:48:55,008 --> 01:48:58,908
a special thing that gets released for anniversary especially.

1896
01:48:59,008 --> 01:49:01,308
Do you guys know what it is?

1897
01:49:01,408 --> 01:49:04,108
Are we going to run the clip? I think we're going to run the clip.

1898
01:49:04,308 --> 01:49:07,608
All right, guys. We have merchandise!

1899
01:49:07,708 --> 01:49:11,208
So I created a little commercial before we get to singing here.

1900
01:49:11,308 --> 01:49:12,908
Run it, staff-san!

1901
01:49:14,708 --> 01:49:20,208
皆ーさん! It's been 5 long years together, but we've done it!
Everyone! It's been 5 long years together, but we've done it!

1902
01:49:20,308 --> 01:49:22,508
We made it to Year 5 together,

1903
01:49:22,608 --> 01:49:25,508
and while the future's looking pretty crazy and eventful,

1904
01:49:25,608 --> 01:49:27,708
let's take a little time to celebrate the story thus far, shall we?

1905
01:49:27,808 --> 01:49:31,208
And what better way to do that than with every Holo's bread and butter,

1906
01:49:31,308 --> 01:49:34,908
the bane of every Dead Beat's wallet's existence?

1907
01:49:35,008 --> 01:49:39,208
That's right, everybody! It's time for premium goods!

1908
01:49:39,308 --> 01:49:41,908
Goods, goods, goods! Yeah, premium goods time.

1909
01:49:42,008 --> 01:49:45,508
You guys know what time it is. You get ready for it every year, right?

1910
01:49:45,608 --> 01:49:49,508
You guys know how I like to release merch that's more on the fashionable side, the practical,

1911
01:49:49,608 --> 01:49:51,708
but I think there are a few things that you guys are going to love here.

1912
01:49:51,808 --> 01:49:55,208
And remember, if you grab it quick and manage to cop the premium limited set,

1913
01:49:55,308 --> 01:49:57,308
you'll get a hand-signed postcard from me!

1914
01:49:57,408 --> 01:50:00,708
Mori Calliope! But like always, supplies are extreme...

1915
01:50:00,356 --> 01:50:02,156
are limited, so don't miss out, okay?

1916
01:50:02,156 --> 01:50:04,256
Okay! Okay! Okay!

1917
01:50:04,356 --> 01:50:06,356
First, we got a poster!

1918
01:50:06,356 --> 01:50:08,856
I mean, you guys expect posters by now, I think.

1919
01:50:08,856 --> 01:50:11,456
You guys are used to posters from me, as every good Dead Beat knows

1920
01:50:11,456 --> 01:50:15,356
Mori Calliope is a poster fan and Mori Calliope fans are fans of posters!

1921
01:50:15,356 --> 01:50:17,656
I see your rooms. I know.

1922
01:50:17,656 --> 01:50:20,456
Not like in a creepy way or anything,

1923
01:50:20,456 --> 01:50:24,156
but this one's a bit smaller than the usual huge posters that I always do for these merch drops,

1924
01:50:24,156 --> 01:50:26,856
but it's to help with the shipping cost this year.

1925
01:50:26,856 --> 01:50:30,156
I don't know, we'll see. Crossing my fingers, but no guarantees.

1926
01:50:30,156 --> 01:50:32,656
Throw it into your cart, see what happens, I guess.

1927
01:50:32,656 --> 01:50:36,756
I went for an Underworld live show concert poster as a concept here,

1928
01:50:36,756 --> 01:50:41,356
and my very own Yukisame-mama created something fun and energetic for the occasion.

1929
01:50:41,356 --> 01:50:45,156
So let's reminisce on the amazing shows that we've gotten to experience together

1930
01:50:45,156 --> 01:50:47,356
with this big-sized poster!

1931
01:50:47,356 --> 01:50:48,656
Yeah, yeah!

1932
01:50:48,656 --> 01:50:51,356
Next up, oh man, this one is big!

1933
01:50:51,356 --> 01:50:55,156
One of my favorite apparel artists, Crisalys, has graced this humble black T-shirt

1934
01:50:55,156 --> 01:50:58,556
with a high quality and subtle design of your Mori,

1935
01:50:58,556 --> 01:51:04,356
dressed in grimoire attire, playing her bass, probably a little badly, in an antique shop!

1936
01:51:04,356 --> 01:51:08,356
It's the type of shirt where you'll probably get, you know, compliments from fellow quirky folks,

1937
01:51:08,356 --> 01:51:13,156
but the average bystander like wouldn't look twice at you kind of deal.

1938
01:51:13,156 --> 01:51:15,856
I don't know, again, I can't guarantee exactly what's going to happen.

1939
01:51:15,856 --> 01:51:19,256
Anyway, you might find Dead Beats out in the wild, too, so that's fun!

1940
01:51:19,256 --> 01:51:23,356
It's just the kind of shirt that subtly expresses your love for Mori Calliope

1941
01:51:23,356 --> 01:51:25,856
without being too, you know, in your face, right?

1942
01:51:25,856 --> 01:51:28,856
And the design is so so so good!

1943
01:51:28,856 --> 01:51:31,856
I owned like five shirts by Crisalys, now I'm about to own six!

1944
01:51:31,856 --> 01:51:34,156
Anyway, don't miss out!

1945
01:51:34,156 --> 01:51:36,856
Next up, it's a Grimoire Plushie!

1946
01:51:36,856 --> 01:51:40,156
Take her everywhere with you! That's what seems to be all the rage these days, right?

1947
01:51:40,156 --> 01:51:43,156
And if you give her a squeeze, she says something!

1948
01:51:43,156 --> 01:51:47,356
I don't know what yet, but maybe we'll all be a little surprised!

1949
01:51:47,356 --> 01:51:51,856
She's got such a cute and huggable design. I'm sure she'll make fast friends with your other plushies,

1950
01:51:51,856 --> 01:51:55,556
especially that weird cat, you know?

1951
01:51:55,556 --> 01:51:58,556
Maybe you can dress her up and put her in a plastic purse for a day out,

1952
01:51:58,556 --> 01:52:01,856
just have fun! I don't know, be whimsical, whatever you want to do!

1953
01:52:01,856 --> 01:52:05,856
Finally, it's a concert and live show staple, a casual wristband!

1954
01:52:05,856 --> 01:52:09,856
Show your support for your Mori in your everyday life or at a local show,

1955
01:52:09,856 --> 01:52:12,356
even if I'm not the one playing!

1956
01:52:12,356 --> 01:52:14,556
Something easy to slip on and fun to rock out with!

1957
01:52:14,556 --> 01:52:17,556
I want to see all of you guys wearing them at my future shows, okay?

1958
01:52:17,556 --> 01:52:20,356
And there's a voice pack, too!

1959
01:52:20,356 --> 01:52:23,856
"Mori Takes a Break"? What kind of title is that?

1960
01:52:23,856 --> 01:52:27,356
Sounds like some fan fiction to me, but give it a listen, I guess.

1961
01:52:27,356 --> 01:52:29,556
Japanese and English voice available.

1962
01:52:29,556 --> 01:52:31,856
日本語もあります！
Japanese is also available!

1963
01:52:31,856 --> 01:52:36,156
Grab the full set and you will get a foil duplicated stamp on a special postcard!

1964
01:52:36,156 --> 01:52:39,856
Be really fast and get your hands on the limited edition set,

1965
01:52:39,856 --> 01:52:44,556
and you might just get your hands on a handwritten autograph from Mori Calliope!

1966
01:52:44,556 --> 01:52:48,856
Actually, it's not that you might, you will get a handwritten autograph from Mori Calliope if you're fast enough!

1967
01:52:49,356 --> 01:52:51,856
We always do gold, though, so how about I sign it with an extra special pink pen?

1968
01:52:51,856 --> 01:52:55,856
I don't know, we'll have to see if they let me. Look forward to it!

1969
01:52:55,856 --> 01:52:59,156
And again, these are limited to a certain amount.

1970
01:52:59,156 --> 01:53:03,556
So if you want to grab a real autograph from your Mori, do not miss out on this chance!

1971
01:53:03,556 --> 01:53:07,856
The sales period will run for about a month, so get your premium goods ASAP, okay?

1972
01:53:07,856 --> 01:53:12,856
It's like a full-on concert hall over here between poster, T-shirt, squeezable mini Mori, and wristband!

1973
01:53:12,856 --> 01:53:17,856
Get ready for lots more shows together, Dead Beats, and thanks for the unforgettable five years!

1974
01:53:18,356 --> 01:53:20,856
Yay! Clap clap clap clap clap!

1975
01:53:20,856 --> 01:53:23,356
I wonder, how much further can we go together?

1976
01:53:23,356 --> 01:53:25,856
I want to see!

1977
01:53:32,356 --> 01:53:33,356
Hello!

1978
01:53:33,356 --> 01:53:37,356
Thank you so much, everybody! I hope that you guys enjoy the goods. Please look forward to receiving them.

1979
01:53:37,356 --> 01:53:42,356
They're very cool! I'm super excited with how they turned out. So make sure that you don't miss it.

1980
01:53:42,356 --> 01:53:48,356
I think the shop will open in about six minutes. You'll be able to pre-order your merch and get the limited if you're quick, you gotta be quick,

1981
01:53:48,356 --> 01:53:53,156
because they do have a limited number. But yeah, please enjoy!

1982
01:53:53,156 --> 01:53:57,356
And thank you always for supporting me so much. There will be a members-only encore after this,

1983
01:53:57,356 --> 01:54:04,856
featuring a few more songs and just getting to chat with my members, which I'm excited about. So please look forward to that.

1984
01:54:05,156 --> 01:54:09,856
And there's a new song! I should look a little happier about that! There's a new song coming out!

1985
01:54:10,356 --> 01:54:14,356
And I haven't really given any hints about what kind of song it is. People are like, "Oh, it's gonna be so emotional, this looks like an emotional song",

1986
01:54:14,356 --> 01:54:21,856
but knowing what the song is makes me laugh really hard because it's actually a lot simpler than you think!

1987
01:54:22,356 --> 01:54:27,856
But something about my early music is that, man, I was so honest, you know?

1988
01:54:28,356 --> 01:54:34,356
And so I wanted to write a song that not just me myself, I as a person could relate to, but anyone,

1989
01:54:34,356 --> 01:54:38,556
anyone who has an oshi could relate to.

1990
01:54:39,356 --> 01:54:44,356
And so, I hope that you will enjoy it, because it feels like an older Mori song,

1991
01:54:44,356 --> 01:54:48,556
while also being a newer Mori song. It's hard to explain,

1992
01:54:48,556 --> 01:54:52,856
but I guess you'll just have to watch it and see. MV's really cute, so we'll watch that.

1993
01:54:52,856 --> 01:54:56,356
Premiere together, too, so don't go anywhere after the credits!

1994
01:54:56,356 --> 01:55:00,356
Please look forward to it! New song, new song! Stream it a lot!

1995
01:55:00,371 --> 01:55:01,671
Watch it lots,

1996
01:55:01,671 --> 01:55:04,571
and, um, share it around. I don't know, if you want, if you like it.

1997
01:55:04,771 --> 01:55:08,871
Um, but I still have one last song memory to replay

1998
01:55:08,871 --> 01:55:11,971
in my mind here in this beautiful area.

1999
01:55:11,971 --> 01:55:14,971
So shall we run it? The last song of today.

2000
01:55:15,271 --> 01:55:16,971
Thank you so much, Deadbeats.

2001
01:55:16,971 --> 01:55:19,771
Catch you on the flip side. There might be an after-credits scene...

2002
01:55:19,771 --> 01:55:21,371
Let's go!

2003
01:55:52,171 --> 01:55:55,571
Lost in thoughts of a frosted frame of mind

2004
01:55:55,571 --> 01:55:57,971
Honest to God, it's just not our time

2005
01:55:57,971 --> 01:56:00,971
Promises flawed by cosmic design

2006
01:56:00,971 --> 01:56:03,871
これくらいどうってことない
It's really no big deal at all,

2007
01:56:03,871 --> 01:56:06,371
でも涙の跡は消せない
but the traces of tears cannot be erased.

2008
01:56:06,371 --> 01:56:09,571
Coming of age, the stage doesn't light up

2009
01:56:09,571 --> 01:56:12,071
Just right away, they told us it might've

2010
01:56:12,071 --> 01:56:15,871
夢はもう諦めます
I'll give up on my dream already.

2011
01:56:16,771 --> 01:56:19,471
This cynical mind says "Why'd you try?"

2012
01:56:19,471 --> 01:56:23,371
"Why not give up and play the bad guy?"

2013
01:56:24,171 --> 01:56:26,871
分かってるさ
I know that.

2014
01:56:27,571 --> 01:56:31,871
運命が波立てながら 貴方飲もうとするのなら
Even if fate stirs up the waves and tries to swallow you whole,

2015
